        "timestamp": 1774439524,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Unclear 'how much of a negotiation is taking place' between US and Iran Middle East Issued on: 25/03/2026 - 12:52 Iran has received a US plan to pause the war in the Middle East, officials said on March 25 — a proposal sent even as Washington deploys paratroopers and more Marines to the region. Tehran did not confirm receiving the plan and publicly dismissed Washington's diplomatic efforts. For FRANCE 24's Philip Turle, a lot of aspects of those negotiations remain unclear: how far have they gone, who is the US dealing with, and what the US is deploying troops in the Middle East for amid as it says it is engaging in negotiations. What do we know of the US's 15-point peace plan sent to Iran? 25/03/2026 Middle East Inside the Palestinian camp in Beirut where residents are staying put, for now 25/03/2026 Middle East In Lebanon, some schools choose to stay open despite the war 25/03/2026 Middle East US ramps up military presence in the Middle East amid reported talks 25/03/2026 Middle East US sends 15-point peace plan to Iran while deploying troops in the region 25/03/2026 Middle East 'The humanitarian crisis here is worsening by the minute': Israel continues to bomb Lebanon 25/03/2026 Middle East US to deploy elite army brigade to Middle East: reports 24/03/2026 Middle East Pakistan’s prime minister says his nation is ready to facilitate talks to end Iran war 24/03/2026 Middle East Saudi leader said to be pushing Trump to continue war in Iran, New York Times reports 24/03/2026 Middle East"
